ology many believe that he may have  originated from a much older germanic  god named tivas who assumed the role of  chief deity that is until he was  replaced in terms of popularity and  authority by odin and thor who would  both share his role as gods of war  the identity of tyr's father is  something that has been questioned over  the years and god of war quite commonly  in norse mythology tyr is one of the  many sons of odin but there are some  sources that claim his father was  instead himir the giant best known for  accompanying thor when they were able to  fish the wild serpent from the bottom of  the ocean  the identity of tyr's mother is  generally unknown as she's never  referred to by name so even though he's  regarded as quite a popular deity there  is still much about tyr that is shrouded  in mystery  despite having quite a large role in  norse mythology tear really features in  any stories the most well known tale  that tyr appears in is the binding of  fenrir  when the wolf fenrir was born the gods  feared that because of how quickly he  grew he would pose a threat to them all  in order for odin and the rest of god to  control fenrir he was raised amongst the  isaiah in asgard but even as a young pup  the early god who dared to approach and  feed him was tyr  eventually it was decided that fenrir  would have to be bound to contain him  and the gods had a variety of chains and  ropes crafted to hold fenrir when fenrir  became suspicious the gods told him that  they were merely testing his strength  applauding him every time he was able to  break free from his bindings  sending word to the dwarven realms they  were able to craft a magical ribbon that  was extremely flexible but could never  be broken regardless of how hard one  struggled  when the gods presented fenrir with this  ribbon the wolf began to suspect  trickery and refused to be bound unless  one of the gods placed their hand in his  jaw as a pledge of good faith  none of the gods were willing to step  forward and volunteer as it would mean  certainly losing her hand  the only one brave enough to step  forward was indeed the just and fearless  tear who without hesitation placed his  hand in fenrir's jaws and as he expected  when fenrir was unable to break free of  the ribbon he chomped down and swallowed  tyr's hand  this story does a fairly good job in  highlighting the selflessness and  bravery of tyr were all of the other  gods were unwilling to lose a hand tier  knowing that binding fenrir would  guarantee the safety of his people was  willing to sacrifice his hand for the  greater good  for the most part tears depiction in god  of all remains fairly true to that of  norse and germanic folklore and tear is  definitely a god that i would have loved  to have seen appearing just more than  paintings but let me know what you guys  think  is tear a god that you had previously  heard of do you think tier may not be  dead at all and we may see him in a  future game  let me know in the comments below  you
 

